Task: Implement the self-contained dead-letter combinator (ADR 0010, Phase 3 Green step).

Summary: DeadLetter[F, K, V].guard(topic, key, value)(process) runs process
with bounded retry, reusing purekafka.resilience.Retry/Guard directly rather
than hand-rolling a second bounded-retry mechanism - the only new behavior
here is what happens on exhaustion (publish (key, value) to <topic>-dlq and
swallow the error, instead of raising). Own purekafka.dlq.published counter
metric, same instrument-naming convention as Phases 1-2.

Split into two layers for testability: DeadLetter.fromPublish takes the
actual "how to send" action as a plain function parameter, so DeadLetterSuite
tests the retry-then-dlq decision logic against a fake recording publish
function with no real Kafka broker involved - same "test the logic, not the
broker" convention this module's other suites already use. DeadLetter.resource
is the real, public, fs2-kafka-backed constructor built on top of fromPublish
- owns its own KafkaProducer.resource internally, callers never construct or
pass one in.

